          "detail": "esptool 5.0.2: use exact chip-specific tokens, not an arbitrary number. MB tokens denote MiB (1048576 bytes); ESP8266 KB tokens denote KiB. ESP8266 also has -c1 layout tokens; ESP32-S2/S3/P4 permit additional larger sizes. keep preserves the image header; detect reads flash ID and the documented detection-failure fallback is 4MB. The default is keep unless ESPTOOL_FS overrides it. These fields apply to a bootable-image header at the chip's bootloader offset; supported sizes depend on chip, ROM/stub and flash hardware. Other releases require verification."
